# Build-context filter for THIS Dockerfile only.
#
# The node-agent build context is the repo root (it has to be, so the image can
# vendor dashboard-api/gpu.py alongside the node-agent sources), and that root
# is ~330 MB including a ~70 MB .git -- all of it uploaded to the daemon for an
# image that needs six .py files and one requirements.txt.
#
# BuildKit reads `<path-to-Dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the
# context root's `.dockerignore`, so this file scopes the filter to the
# node-agent build and leaves every other build in the repo untouched. Compose
# v2 uses BuildKit by default; with the legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) this
# file is ignored and the build merely falls back to being slow.
#
# Allowlist: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what the Dockerfile
# COPYs.
**

!ods/extensions/services/node-agent/requirements.txt
!ods/extensions/services/node-agent/*.py
!ods/extensions/services/dashboard-api/gpu.py
